---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'ProfilePage',
    name: 'About Ahsan Tariq',
    url: `${site.url}/about`,
    mainEntity: {
      '@type': 'Person',
      name: site.name,
      jobTitle: 'Team Lead',
      url: site.url,
      image: `${site.url}/ahsan-tariq.jpg`,
      worksFor: { '@type': 'Organization', name: site.company, url: site.companyUrl },
      alumniOf: { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: site.education.institution },
      award: `${site.award.text}, ${site.award.date}`,
      address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressLocality: 'Lahore', addressCountry: 'PK' },
      email: `mailto:${site.email}`,
      sameAs: [site.github, site.linkedin],
      knowsAbout: [
        'PostgreSQL',
        'Query optimisation',
        'Elasticsearch',
        'Algolia',
        'FastAPI',
        'Python',
        'Data pipelines',
        'Data engineering',
      ],
    },
  },
];

const skills = [
  { group: 'Languages', items: ['Python', 'SQL', 'Ruby'] },
  { group: 'Frameworks & APIs', items: ['FastAPI', 'Ruby on Rails', 'REST API design'] },
  { group: 'Data', items: ['PostgreSQL', 'Redis', 'Elasticsearch', 'Algolia'] },
  { group: 'Async & pipelines', items: ['Celery', 'Background workers', 'Retries & idempotency'] },
  {
    group: 'Engineering',
    items: [
      'Query optimisation',
      'Index design',
      'Transactional integrity',
      'Data modelling',
      'Testing',
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About — Ahsan Tariq, team lead and software engineer"
  description="Software engineer and team lead at A'sTechware in Lahore. B.Sc. Computer Science, UET Lahore (Narowal Campus), CGPA 3.734 / 4.00. Why I am moving toward data engineering and machine learning."
  ogType="profile"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="container page-head page-head--split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Software engineer and team lead, focused on backend and data systems.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I am Ahsan Tariq. I work at A'sTechware in Lahore, Pakistan — associate software engineer from
        July 2024, software engineer since September 2025, and team lead since June 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="portrait">
      <img
        src="/ahsan-tariq.jpg"
        alt="Portrait of Ahsan Tariq"
        width="400"
        height="400"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
  </div>

  <section class="container section--tight">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I started on the API side and moved toward the parts of the stack where correctness is
        decided: the schema, the query plan, the transaction boundary. That is where the interesting
        failures live. A feature can look finished in a demo and still be selling the same tee time
        twice.
      </p>
      <p>
        At A'sTechware I have worked on Golfpay, The Grants Hub, Restaurant Resource and Serva. The
        features differ; the underlying work is similar: keep the data correct under concurrency,
        keep queries fast as the data grows, and make it explainable when a number changes.
      </p>
      <p>
        On Serva I am the main backend lead. The product's output is a legal document: an intake
        pipeline reads instruction emails and court PDFs, an affidavit is assembled from recorded
        field facts, and billing is derived from logged attempts. Working on a system where a
        plausible guess is worse than a missing field changed how I think about AI features.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--plain">At a glance</p>
        <h2>Experience and education</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="mono muted"><a href="/background">Full background →</a></p>
    </div>
    <dl class="metrics">
      <div class="metric">
        <dt>Now</dt>
        <dd>Team Lead, A'sTechware (since June 2026)</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="metric">
        <dt>Before</dt>
        <dd>Software Engineer (since September 2025); Associate Software Engineer (July 2024 – September 2025)</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="metric">
        <dt>Education</dt>
        <dd>B.Sc. Computer Science, UET Lahore (Narowal Campus), 2020 – 2024, CGPA 3.734 / 4.00</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="container section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--plain">Toolkit</p>
        <h2>What I work with</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="skills">
      {skills.map((group) => (
        <div class="skill-group">
          <h3>{group.group}</h3>
          <ul>
            {group.items.map((item) => <li class="tag">{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--plain">Motivation</p>
        <h2>Why data engineering, and why this programme</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I want to strengthen my foundations in data engineering and machine learning. My practical
        experience is in the layer that makes AI output usable: pipelines, review steps, retries and
        audit trails. What I do not have yet is the formal foundation underneath it — query
        optimisation as theory rather than instinct, data warehousing, statistics, and machine
        learning beyond coursework and one final-year project.
      </p>
      <p>
        The two-year structure is the reason I am applying to this programme rather than a
        single-country master: fundamentals at ULB and UPC, a summer school, then a specialisation
        and a thesis with industry or a research lab.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am interested in evaluation and data quality for extraction pipelines: how per-field
        accuracy is measured on a labelled sample, how a review threshold is chosen when a false
        positive and a false negative cost different amounts, and how human corrections are kept
        from degrading the record over time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Production work has shown me why AI features need retries, review steps and audit trails.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <div class="container cta__grid">
      <div>
        <h2>Happy to go deeper on any of this.</h2>
        <p>
          If you are reviewing my DEAI application, the case studies are the fastest way into the
          technical side. Transcripts, references and the motivation letter carry the formal case —
          this site is a supplement to them, not a substitute.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="btn-row cta__actions">
        <a class="btn" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email me</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/background">Background</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
